{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And it was morning, and behold she is Leah.</b> This verse teaches us Jacob's modesty, that he did not talk much, even with his wife — for had he spoken with her, he would have recognized her by her voice, since he had already dwelt with her seven years. And if you ask: but they were betrothed in error, for he thought she was Rachel? One may answer: once he knew she was Leah, he married her for the sake of betrothal."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:37.046677115Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}